## ADR-0023 execution-budget correction

Approved ADR-0023 identified a latent defect in the frozen provider boundary: request-local `maxTurns` and `maxOutputTokens` did not prove cumulative execution limits. The bounded correction adds the `execution-budget-conformance` local gate and the metadata-only attestation at `agent-platform/baselines/execution-budget-conformance-2026-08-25.json`. Exact candidate identity remains owned by `ci:prepublish` through its tree binding; this attestation does not substitute for that gate.

The correction makes the direct Claude Messages HTTP and OpenAI Responses HTTP paths conformant, and makes Codex CLI fail closed before subprocess execution. Round-3 recovery now preserves an independent `UNRESOLVED` remote-invocation fact after conservative accounting and denies another generation until terminal execution is durably proven; heartbeat/takeover and evidence append share one filesystem authority lock with monotonic fence-history validation. It does not reinterpret role-level agentic turns, alter role values, add a provider or router, enable OpenCode/Groq, register a harness, build a gateway, or authorize deployment/release. The earlier live Codex CLI baselines remain truthful historical evidence of the behavior observed before ADR-0023; they are not evidence that the CLI satisfies the newly approved hard-budget contract.

## External observation

The refreshed read-only GitHub observation on August 9, 2026 found a public repository and an active `Protect main` ruleset with pull requests, resolved conversations, signed commits, CodeQL, deletion/non-fast-forward protection, no bypass actors, and the required `Agent platform / contracts-policy-evals` job. Closure-hardening PR #32 passed every required check and merged as `7dc157d2f84670145c4f1b5fcba274cf06f6f4dc`.

Preview, staging, and production environments exist. Production has a custom branch policy and administrator bypass is disabled, but it has no required reviewer. The `agent-evals` environment does not exist. These facts are recorded without secrets in `agent-platform/baselines/external-controls-observation-2026-08-09.json`.

The representative Codex evidence remains preserved in `agent-platform/baselines/live-codex-representative-2026-08-09.json`. A separate accepted aggregate in `agent-platform/baselines/live-codex-multiscenario-2026-08-09.json` binds six successful ChatGPT-authenticated Codex CLI runs to candidate `e27ddcb7026059b48c5e97277c6e9d386511b8a5`: `bounded-typescript-bug` and `documentation-only-change`, each repeated three times with distinct WorkUnit, AgentRun, ProviderRun, and EvalResult correlations. Task success and evidence completeness are 1.0 with zero tool calls, retries, security failures, or scope violations. Prompts, responses, credentials, provider metadata, unmeasured cost, and unperformed independent provider review are not claimed; no tuning was applied. These risk-0 evals do not require cross-provider council evidence, and no Claude run is claimed.

The exact merge candidate was built and attested in PR-quality run `31342391343`. Independent `gh attestation verify` enforcement bound `beacon-dist.tar.gz` digest `f4ff3b08a96f2e89640710771f263e6a60ab0dfae43d62b6a56b7e415be9d7ed` to `.github/workflows/pr-quality.yml`, `refs/heads/main`, and the merge SHA. Staging run `31342520379` verified and promoted that same artifact as Worker version `3e4de117-f432-4a3a-b3fd-aecedf295c9f`; post-deploy run `31342578773` then passed the live status and security-header checks. The bounded promotion and verification records are artifacts `9046260894` and `9046271178`.

The ruleset hardening and known-good rollback drill closed in "Record ruleset hardening and known-good rollback drill evidence" (#50): `strict_required_status_checks_policy` is enabled and the `prepublish` check context is required, verified live via merged PR #47 (its pre-merge evidence tree matched post-merge `main`'s tree exactly, and `authorize-publication.mjs` independently returned `PUBLICATION AUTHORIZED`). The rollback drill deployed a distinct, independently attested prior artifact (commit `ae7cc8f16fea5f714f68cf4a62da85a692985c4a`) to staging (workflow `31457446664`), and recovery verification found a real, honest regression — that artifact predates `run_worker_first`, so static assets bypassed `src/worker.ts`'s header injection and `post-deploy-verify.yml` correctly failed (`31457577664`). Staging was then restored to commit `7dc157d2f84670145c4f1b5fcba274cf06f6f4dc` (workflow `31457642967`, success) and headers were reverified present by direct curl.

Production promotion and verification closed in "Record production promotion and verification evidence" (#51): that same fully-evidenced artifact was promoted to the live `beaconco9` Worker via `deploy-production.yml` (workflow `31458088053`, success) with no rebuild step, and independently reverified via `post-deploy-verify.yml` (workflow `31458458241`, success). Both runs received the real, non-bypassable production-environment review, approved by the repository owner directly in the GitHub UI in both cases — not simulated or bypassed by any agent. Verified live: matching sha256 and GitHub attestation on the deployed artifact, an identical etag (`888ce5acc6d70c7b2e6b1597d7e9e1cc`) between production and staging, and all required security headers present via direct curl against `https://beaconco9.beaconco57.workers.dev/` and via `post-deploy-verify.yml`'s own formal check.

## Hard gates — all closed

All seven Phase 1.5 evidence gates (`representativeLiveProviderRun`, `repeatedLiveEvalBaseline`, `agentPlatformRequiredCheck`, `verifiedBuildAttestation`, `stagingPromotionAndVerification`, `knownGoodRollbackDrill`, `productionPromotionAndVerification`) are `true` in `agent-platform/baselines/external-controls-observation-2026-08-09.json` (refreshed through PR #50 and #51, `observedMainSha: b70959170c30599e4eab241ac5e8dc2e208d1091`) and independently confirmed by the live `npm run phase15:audit` re-run cited above.

Non-bypassable external production approval is closed. Production administrator bypass is disabled, and the environment has one required reviewer (self-review not prevented). A separate, previously-undocumented bypass path was found and closed earlier the same day: the Cloudflare native Git integration for the `beaconco9` Worker auto-deployed independent of this GitHub environment gate. It was manually disconnected and the disconnect was empirically verified — merging a trivial change to `main` produced zero Workers Builds check-runs and no change to the live production `etag`.

## Freeze rule

This page changes to complete/frozen only once `npm run phase15:audit` passes using real reviewed evidence — it now does, per the literal command output cited in the Audit conclusion above, re-verified live at commit `7c5eff1736612d1e33dc4082c959e6bf61ce9f1d` immediately before this edit. Workflow definitions, synthetic adapter responses, deterministic fixtures, and unverified external settings never satisfy live gates on their own; only the live audit re-run does. Re-run the command again before trusting this page in a future session — per the Phase 1.6 master spec's freshness discipline, this is a timestamped observation, not a durable fact.
